# Performance Optimization Guide

## Quick Performance Checklist

When adding new features or modifying existing code, verify:

### Rendering
- [ ] Using instancing for repeated objects (not individual meshes)
- [ ] LOD system enabled for complex geometry
- [ ] Shaders compiled to TSL, not raw GLSL
- [ ] Unnecessary draw calls eliminated (batch when possible)
- [ ] Textures atlased or compressed with Draco
- [ ] Fog/bloom effects limited to visible area

### Physics
- [ ] Collision shapes simplified (box/sphere, not mesh)
- [ ] Sleeping bodies properly configured
- [ ] Raycast queries cached/throttled
- [ ] Physics update rate synchronized with render

### Memory
- [ ] Disposed geometries/materials on cleanup
- [ ] No memory leaks from event listeners
- [ ] Texture atlasing to reduce VRAM usage
- [ ] Resource pooling for frequently created objects

### Mobile Specific
- [ ] Quality settings adapted for low-end devices
- [ ] Touch events debounced/throttled
- [ ] Canvas resolution adaptive
- [ ] No memory spike from resource loading

## Profiling Tools

### Browser DevTools
```
F12 → Performance tab
1. Record for 5-10 seconds
2. Zoom on the timeline
3. Look for:
   - Long frames (>16ms for 60 FPS)
   - GPU stalls
   - GC pauses
```

### Three.js Stats
```javascript
// In Experience.js or Debug.js
import Stats from 'three/examples/jsm/libs/stats.min.js';
const stats = new Stats();
document.body.appendChild(stats.dom);

// In animation loop
stats.update();
```

### WebGPU Specific
```javascript
// Check shader compilation time
const adapter = await navigator.gpu?.requestAdapter();
const device = await adapter?.requestDevice();
console.time('shader-compile');
// ... create material ...
console.timeEnd('shader-compile');
```

## Common Bottlenecks & Solutions

### High CPU Usage

**Symptom**: 60 FPS but CPU throttled

| Issue | Solution |
|-------|----------|
| Too many draw calls | Use instancing, batch, combine meshes |
| Physics queries | Cache raycasts, throttle checks |
| Animation loops | Move to GPU, use GPU instancing |
| Large geometries | Implement LOD, culling |

### High GPU Usage

**Symptom**: GPU at 100%, performance drops in complex areas

| Issue | Solution |
|-------|----------|
| Overdraw | Reduce particle count, optimize shaders |
| Fill rate | Lower resolution, reduce effects |
| Texture bandwidth | Compress, use atlasing, mipmap |
| Large buffers | Stream data, use dynamic buffers |

### Memory Spikes

**Symptom**: Sudden FPS drop, GC pause

| Issue | Solution |
|-------|----------|
| Loading resources | Lazy load, stream, preload in background |
| Allocating arrays | Use typed arrays, object pooling |
| String concatenation | Pre-allocate strings, use template literals |
| Event listeners | Always clean up, remove on destroy |

## Optimization Strategies by System

### Grass Rendering (Millions of Blades)

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT - Instanced
const geometry = new THREE.PlaneGeometry(width, height);
const material = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial();
const instancedMesh = new THREE.InstancedMesh(geometry, material, count);

// ❌ WRONG - Individual meshes
for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {
  const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geometry, material);
  scene.add(mesh);
}
```

### Terrain LOD

```javascript
// Use distance-based LOD
const distance = camera.position.distanceTo(terrainPosition);
if (distance < 50) {
  terrain.setDetail('high');     // Full resolution
} else if (distance < 200) {
  terrain.setDetail('medium');   // 50% vertices
} else {
  terrain.setDetail('low');      // 10% vertices
}
```

### Shader Optimization

```javascript
// ✅ EFFICIENT - Minimal operations
const colorNode = texture(baseMap).mul(color(diffuse));

// ❌ INEFFICIENT - Multiple samples
const c1 = texture(map1);
const c2 = texture(map2);
const c3 = texture(map3);
const final = c1.mul(c2).add(c3);
```

### Physics Optimization

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT - Sleeping, simple shapes
const body = world.createRigidBody(RigidBodyDesc.fixed());
const shape = ColliderDesc.box(1, 1, 1);
body.sleep();  // Put to sleep if inactive

// ❌ WRONG - Complex mesh collider, always active
const collider = ColliderDesc.trimesh(vertices, indices);
body.wakeUp();
```

## Adaptive Quality System

The project uses `Quality.js` to automatically scale:

```javascript
// Based on FPS monitoring
if (avgFps < 30) {
  quality.decrease();  // Lower resolution, disable effects
} else if (avgFps > 50) {
  quality.increase();  // Higher resolution, more effects
}
```

Settings adjusted:
1. **Shadow Resolution**: 512px → 256px
2. **Particle Count**: 100% → 50% → 25%
3. **LOD Distances**: Increased (objects disappear sooner)
4. **Bloom**: Off → Quarter resolution → Full
5. **Canvas Resolution**: Full → 3/4 → 1/2

## Network & Asset Optimization

### Model Loading
```javascript
// ✅ Use Draco compression
const loader = new GLTFLoader();
const dracoLoader = new DRACOLoader();
loader.setDRACOLoader(dracoLoader);

// ❌ Avoid uncompressed large files
```

### Texture Optimization
```javascript
// ✅ Compress and optimize
// Use PNG for non-transparent, WebP if supported
// Add mipmaps for all textures
texture.generateMipmaps = true;
texture.magFilter = THREE.LinearFilter;
texture.minFilter = THREE.LinearMipmapLinearFilter;
```

## Mobile-Specific Optimizations

### Orientation Handling
```javascript
window.addEventListener('orientationchange', () => {
  camera.aspect = innerWidth / innerHeight;
  camera.updateProjectionMatrix();
  renderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);
});
```

### Touch Event Throttling
```javascript
let lastTouchTime = 0;
canvas.addEventListener('touchmove', (e) => {
  const now = Date.now();
  if (now - lastTouchTime < 16) return;  // 60 FPS cap
  lastTouchTime = now;
  // ... handle touch ...
});
```

### Battery & CPU Optimization
```javascript
// Reduce updates when not focused
document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () => {
  if (document.hidden) {
    renderer.setAnimationLoop(null);  // Stop rendering
  } else {
    renderer.setAnimationLoop(animate);
  }
});
```

## Benchmarking

Target FPS by device:
- **High-end Desktop** (RTX 3080): 144 FPS target
- **Mid-range Desktop** (RTX 2070): 60 FPS target
- **Low-end Laptop** (Intel UHD): 30 FPS target
- **Tablet** (iPad Pro): 60 FPS target
- **Mobile** (iPhone 15): 30 FPS target
- **Old Mobile** (iPhone 12): 20 FPS target

